# 000-NET-0048 — `get`, an analog of `wget` and `curl` — done

**Type:** network (a new program `get`) · **Owner:** `NET` · **Priority:** P2 · **Status:** done (2026-11-09) · **Blocked by:** — · **Main task:** — · **Constitution:** MC-3.1, MC-11.6, MC-11.11, MC-12.1

Recorded by the network track on 2026-10-25, for the plan [docs/communications-and-agents.md](../docs/communications-and-agents.md), at the maintainer's request: "an analog of wget/curl".

## Problem

- **The shell's `fetch` and `https`** take one URL and print or save what comes.
- **Nothing sends a POST, sets a header, uploads a file, follows a redirect, or tests an API** from the console or a script.

## Plan

**The program `get`** (its name is the maintainer's to change), a process of its own:

- **What it does:**
  - `get URL` prints the body;
  - `-o FILE` saves it, within the program's scope; `-O` saves it under the URL's last segment;
  - `-c` resumes;
  - `-I` shows the head only;
  - `-X METHOD`, `-H 'Name: value'`, `-d TEXT` or `-d @FILE`, `-F name=@FILE` (multipart);
  - `-L` follows redirects (on by default, `--max-redirs N`);
  - `-s` is silent; `-w` prints the status and the time;
  - `--max-time S`;
  - `-u user` asks for the password on the console, never takes it from the command line.
- **How it reaches a host:**
  - HTTPS through the shell's TLS client, with `BADGE_TLS_NO_DEVICE`;
  - plain HTTP only with `--insecure-http`, said on the console.
- **Its authority:**
  - a flow grant for the URL's host and port, asked of the user at run time (000-NET-0049);
  - a VFS scope of the current directory for `-o`, `-d @` and `-F`;
  - nothing else.
- **The exit status** follows `curl`'s for the common cases (0 success, 6 no such host, 7 no connection, 22 an HTTP error with `-f`, 28 a timeout), so that scripts read it.
- **`fetch` and `https` stay** as they are; `get` is for everything beyond one GET.

## Acceptance criteria

- **Host tests:** the argument parser, the exit statuses.
- **In QEMU, x86 and aarch64** (a `get` suite against 000-NET-0047's stand-in server):
  - a GET to the console and to a file;
  - a resume after a cut;
  - a JSON POST from a file;
  - a multipart upload;
  - a redirect chain;
  - a refused certificate;
  - a host the user refuses.
- **The shell's `help get`** and docs/network.

## Progress (2026-10-28)

**Made** by the kernel track, for this open track's task (AGENTS.md section 5), with 000-NET-0045 and 000-NET-0049:

- **`get/`**, a process of its own (`get/src/args.rs`: the words split as a shell splits them, the options, curl's exit
  statuses; `get/src/main.rs`: the request). In `02_build.sh`'s programs, so in both images.
- **Options:** `-o`, `-O` (into `ram:`), `-c`, `-I`, `-X GET|POST|PUT`, `-H`, `-d TEXT|@FILE`, `-F name=value|name=@FILE`,
  `-L` (default), `--no-location`, `--max-redirs N` (10 at most), `-s`, `-w`, `-f`, `-m`/`--max-time`, `--insecure-http`.
  Credentials (`Authorization`, `Cookie`, `Proxy-Authorization`) are not sent on to another host or port after a
  redirect.
- **Its authority, apart from the plan:**
  - the files are the shell's client of the user's files (`REQUEST_FILES`: `ram:`, `data/`, `log:`), not a scope of the
    current directory: `REQUEST_FILE` scopes the directory of the program's first argument only, and `get`'s files may
    be any of its arguments;
  - the hosts are the policy's lines for `get` (a host and port, or a browsing grant, 000-NET-0049), not yet one asked of
    the user at run time.
- **Exit statuses:** 0, 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 22, 23, 26, 28, 35, 47, 56, 60, curl's numbers.
- **Tested:**
  - host: `tests/get_host.rs` (5 tests: the words, every option, what is refused, `-O`'s name, the statuses), in
    `scripts/host_tests.sh`;
  - QEMU, x86 and aarch64, the `net` suite's download check (`get_runs`), against `tests/http_api_stub.py` (an echo, a
    redirect to the same host and to another, a slow answer added) and the release server over HTTPS. The list is in
    [docs/network/downloads.md](../docs/network/downloads.md#tested).
- **Docs:** [docs/network/downloads.md](../docs/network/downloads.md#get), README; `help get` is the program's own text.

**Left, so the issue stays open:**

- `-u user`, the password asked on the console;
- a host the user refuses at run time: 000-NET-0049's question, which waits for the shell (APP);
- `-I` asks with GET and reads no body, and `-X` has no HEAD, PATCH or DELETE: `mind::http::Method` has GET, POST and
  PUT only (000-NET-0047; effector's exhaustive `match` on it is recorded in `requests-EFF.md`).

## Progress (2026-10-29)

In `main` at ef3faf0d (landing round 41, the request's commit 3f4fa0aa): `get` and its host tests (`tests/get_host.rs`), and the `net` suite's `get_runs` against `tests/http_api_stub.py`, passed in the round 41 gate on x86 and aarch64 (the `net` suite runs in "x86: boot, display, network, TLS, shell, memory, clock", "aarch64: files, network and TLS" and the other aarch64 groups).

Still left: what the Progress section lists (`-u`, a host refused at run time, HEAD, PATCH and DELETE).

## Progress (2026-11-06)

**HEAD, PATCH and DELETE** were done with 000-NET-0047 (f7fd71f5, 2026-10-30): `-I` sends HEAD and `-X` takes the three;
the `get_runs` check covers them. That item of the list above was left there.

**A host asked at run time, on `claude/youthful-mendel-mf1soy`** (000-NET-0049's `socket.wit` 2.8, the shell's question
from 000-APP-0120):
- a connection or a name's lookup the grant refuses (`Denied`) becomes a question through the grant, with the reason
  `the URL on its command line` (or `a redirect from …`). The URL itself is not sent, as its query may hold a token;
- the answer's address is connected to; `N` or no answer: exit 7, `REFUSED BY THE USER`;
- `get` waits on the question up to `--max-time`, and 90 s at most (the broker refuses it at 60 s);
- **tested** in QEMU, `get_runs`: a stand-in on a port the policy does not give `get`, with `get` in front of the serial
  console; refused with `N`, allowed with `O` and its body fetched.

**What waits for the shell (APP), numbered by APP on 2026-11-08:**
- **`-u user`:** [000-APP-0126](000-APP-0126-a-console-program-reads-a-secret.done). `get` is a console program: the shell keeps the keys typed while it runs (Esc and Ctrl+C stop it,
  `Shell::key`), so it cannot read a password from the console. A first version read the keys itself and was taken
  out when the `get_runs` check showed that none arrived.
- **A question from a script:** [000-APP-0125](000-APP-0125-a-scripts-program-asks-about-a-flow.done). `msh`'s wait on its program (`ShellHost::run`) does not put the question, so a
  script's `get` to a host its grant does not name is refused at 60 s (exit 7).

**Left:** those two, once the shell gives them.

**Landed (2026-11-06).** Round 89 (`main` 5ef99d16): the gate was green on every group, the `net` suite's `get_runs`
with the question among them, on x86 and aarch64.

## Progress (2026-11-09)

**`-u USER` without a password,** on `claude/youthful-mendel-mf1soy`, through the shell's secret line (`shell.wit` 1.12, 000-APP-0126, in `main` since round 102):
- `get` asks for `REQUEST_SECRET_LINE`. The shell lends a console program in front of a console a copy of its client badged for that call alone, in `SLOT_SHELL`.
- **The prompt** is `PASSWORD FOR USER AT HOST`, cut to the 80 bytes the shell takes. The shell names the program and its PID before it, and the line is typed with no echo.
- **The answer:**
  - the bytes are built into the `Authorization` header, and `get`'s copy is wiped;
  - Esc: exit 2, `NO PASSWORD TYPED (REFUSED AT THE CONSOLE)`;
  - a script's `get`, which gets no such copy: exit 2, `NO CONSOLE TO TYPE IT AT (A SCRIPT): GIVE USER:PASSWORD`.
- **`help get`** says so, and no longer says a script's `get` is not asked about a host (000-APP-0125 did that).
- **Tested** in QEMU, the `net` suite's `get_runs`: x86 in the kernel session's container (QEMU 8.2.2, TCG, 4 CPUs; the whole suite, 39 checks), aarch64 on acc-1 through Effector (the group "aarch64: network, TLS and Effector", at 1012596d):
  - `-u alice:s3:cr` sent as Basic authentication, and not sent on to another port;
  - `-u alice` with a password typed at the serial console (a space and a non-ASCII letter in it): sent as Basic authentication, and in no line of the serial console or of the shell's log;
  - Esc refused it (2), and a script's `get -u alice` was refused (2).
  - The host tests: `get_host` (6).

**Left:** the gate. With it, the issue's criteria are met but for the plan's VFS scope of the current directory, which the shell's client of the user's files replaced (Progress of 2026-10-28).

## Resolution

**All criteria are met. Its last item, `-u USER` with the password typed at the console, landed in round 103 (`main` a927f175, 2026-11-09).**
- **`get`** (`get/`), a process of its own:
  - `-o`, `-O`, `-c`, `-I`, `-X` (GET, POST, PUT, HEAD, PATCH, DELETE), `-H`, `-d`, `-F`, `-L` and `--max-redirs`, `-s`, `-w`, `-f`, `--max-time`, `--insecure-http`;
  - `-u USER:PASSWORD`, or `-u USER` with the password typed at its console with no echo through the shell's secret line (000-APP-0126);
  - curl's exit statuses.
- **Its authority:**
  - the hosts its flow grant names, and a host it does not name asked of the user at run time (000-NET-0049), from a script too (000-APP-0125);
  - the user's files through the shell's client (`REQUEST_FILES`), in place of the plan's scope of the current directory (the reason is in the Progress of 2026-10-28).
- **Evidence:**
  - the host tests (`tests/get_host.rs`, 6);
  - the `net` suite's `get_runs` on x86 and aarch64, against `tests/http_api_stub.py` and the release server: every case of the criteria, and `-u` typed, refused with Esc and refused in a script;
  - every group of round 103's gate.

  QEMU's runs say nothing of a machine's network (MC-12.1).
- **Not done:** nothing the issue asked for. One remark for the core of `libmind`: the generated binding's buffer that carried the typed line (`mind::idl::shell::secret_line`) is freed when the call returns, not wiped first; `get` wipes only its own copy.

